cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Scientific Writing Skills: a Claude plugin distilled from Writing in the Sciences"
message: "If you use this plugin in work you publish, please cite it, and please cite the course it derives from."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sosa
    given-names: David
    alias: dvdsosa
repository-code: "https://github.com/dvdsosa/scientific-writing-skills"
url: "https://github.com/dvdsosa/scientific-writing-skills"
abstract: >-
  Six AI skills and four analysis scripts for scientific writing, derived from
  all eight units of Stanford's Writing in the Sciences (Kristin Sainani). Covers
  sentence and paragraph editing, IMRaD manuscript structure, the writing
  process, publication ethics and peer review, grant proposals and letters, and
  communication with general audiences.
keywords:
  - scientific writing
  - academic writing
  - manuscript editing
  - IMRaD
  - peer review
  - grant writing
  - science communication
  - large language models
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-08"
references:
  - type: generic
    title: "Writing in the Sciences"
    authors:
      - family-names: Sainani
        given-names: Kristin
    institution:
      name: Stanford University
    url: "https://online.stanford.edu/courses/som-y0010-writing-sciences"
    notes: "The source course. All pedagogical credit belongs here."
